DECISION: stopping all automated GGUF conversion attempts. The memory spike during the write phase happens faster than a 5-second polling loop can reliably react to, and no memory-cap/self-kill strategy tried so far has prevented a crash. This is not a "tune the parameters more" problem - it needs a fundamentally different approach or explicit human supervision, not another automated retry.
Current verified state: system stable, 25GB available, no leftover processes. The already-merged 15GB safetensors model at finetuning/parse_query_gguf/ is untouched and intact. No training was lost. Only the final safetensors->GGUF conversion step remains undone.
